  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.2.2-rc.1: SCTP backpressure + duplicate-handshake hardening. (1) RtcPeer.Send now awaits OnBufferedAmountLow when the data channel's BufferedAmount exceeds MaxBufferedAmount (64 KB) before pushing more bytes, preventing User-Initiated Abort (sctpCauseCode=12) on the remote end during multi-MB push-back (e.g. 1 MB+ tensor result buffers in P2P compute pipelines). (2) Torrent.OnHandshake duplicate-detection now skips the destroy when either ChannelName label is empty/falls back to the per-side peer.Id - those labels are not cross-side stable, so applying the rule could destroy opposing wires bilaterally and kill the connection. Both wires live in that case; consumer-layer dedup (e.g. P2PWebRtcBridge) collapses them by remote BitTorrent peer id.",
